Changes with the next minor release

    *) Prepare the module for release with one hosted-only pull-request CI
       entry point, preserved Linux/Windows compatibility coverage, native
       static-analysis profiles, 32-bit atomic controls, a gzip fuzz target,
       dependency/license checks and contributor/linter documentation.

    *) In the literal-signature engine, normalize raw plus signs as spaces only
       in request/proxy-target queries and form-urlencoded bodies while
       preserving percent-encoded plus signs. Reduce false positives by
       excluding sensitive-file matches from Referer, requiring contextual
       Java object/array-stream and PHP webshell filename signatures, and
       retaining compiled true/false-positive corpus controls.

    *) Bound the common gzip inspection allocation to a 64 KiB decoded prefix,
       retrying at the configured decoded-body cap only when the prefix fills.

    *) Add opt-in shield_gzip request inspection using bounded zlib decoding,
       independent encoded/decoded inspection budgets, unchanged forwarded
       compressed bodies and incomplete-inspection counters.

    *) Add an optional bounded deployment checker for declared Shield coverage,
       PHP/final-handoff mappings, private destinations and internal routes,
       with safe diagnostics and explicit unsupported-input outcomes.

    *) Add an optional native PHP boundary recipe with approved absolute
       entrypoints, non-executable filesystem trees and recording FastCGI tests
       for nginx and Angie. No module runtime changes.

    *) Add a native private-destination recipe using separate worker/backend
       ownership and filesystem permissions, with real nginx/Angie tests for
       aliases, redirects, symlinks, hardlinks and public file identity.

    *) Add optional http-context shield_stats_zone <name> <size> for global
       counters without banning. shield_ban_status accepts either zone kind.
       Ban shared-memory layout remains unchanged by this addition.

    *) Allow ?format=json|prometheus to override the status format. Metrics
       now default to Prometheus 0.0.4; OpenMetrics 1.0 requires an explicit
       acceptable application/openmetrics-text Accept header. Successful
       status responses include Vary: Accept. JSON remains the default.

    *) Split category detections by detect and block mode in status output.

    *) Add inspected-request, active-ban refusal, eviction and allocation-failure
       counters, plus reserved and total ban-zone byte gauges, to JSON and
       OpenMetrics status output.

    *) The ban-zone shared-memory layout has changed. Stop nginx completely and
       restart it when upgrading from an earlier module binary. A configuration
       reload or live binary upgrade cannot migrate existing shared zones.
       Ordinary configuration reloads with the same binary retain all counters.
